# Keep LF line endings on everything that gets executed or parsed by a Linux
# tool, whatever platform it was checked out on.
#
# Windows git defaults to core.autocrlf=true and rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout. A shell script that has been through that fails in bash with
#
#     ./infra/rebuild.sh: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which names neither line endings nor Windows, and happens even inside WSL
# where the script is otherwise perfectly runnable. The same carriage returns
# break a Caddyfile directive and a .env value silently — a trailing \r ends up
# inside the password.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf
Caddyfile*  text eol=lf
.env*       text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
